# Reference only. A static site needs no variables to run, and Dockhold never
# reads a committed .env — set anything you need in the dashboard.
#
# PORT is provided by Dockhold at runtime — don't set it yourself; the start
# script reads it (serve -l $PORT .).
#
# If your HTML/JS needs config, fetch it at runtime or inject it when the
# container starts — don't commit it into the build. Never put secrets in a
# static site: anything served to the browser is public.
